# Task command center workflow

When work involves **TASKS.md**, a **Jira epic/ticket**, a **Slack thread**, **Google Docs**, or **multiple repos**, do not jump straight to coding on `main`.

**Read and follow the `task-command-center` skill** (source:
`fyodoriv/agentbrew/skill-plugins/workflow/task-command-center/SKILL.md`).

Minimum sequence:

1. **`load-project-context`** in each repo you will touch.
2. **Intake** → `SYNC-STATUS.md`, `LINKS.md`, Slack/Jira/Drive mirrors.
3. **Command-center worktree** → `~/apps/{repo}-command-center` on `docs/{project}-command-center`; draft **DO NOT MERGE** PR.
4. **Plan** → `plans/implementation-plan.md` per assigned ticket. Read `writing-plans` and `task-command-center` → `references/implementation-plan-template.md`; lead with overall goal/vision and alternatives, distinguish facts from proposals, and give every numbered task a Why, dependencies/parallelism, acceptance evidence, and verification.
5. **Dry run** → separate `~/apps/{repo}-dry-run` worktree; log in `plans/dry-run-log.md`.
6. **Execute** → main checkout feature branches with repo delivery and verification skills.

**Recurring reconciliation (IRON LAW):** whenever a refresh touches a Google Doc and either a docs PR or Jira, run `task-command-center` → `references/reconciliation-protocol.md`. Read all GDoc tabs/comments, the PR, the epic, and every child first. Keep each child description split into **Product contract (immutable)** with source citations and **Engineering guidance (dynamic)**. Transient status/lane/scheduling belongs in Jira fields or dated comments, not description rewrites. Re-read every destination after writes.

**Jira scope (IRON LAW):** Jira fields and links own the parent, epic,
initiative, type, status, assignee, estimate, priority, sprint, and development
metadata. Do not repeat them in descriptions. Never state PR or branch status
there. A user-requested single-PR delivery means one canonical ticket and one
delivery PR; link and close redundant issues as duplicates. Honor explicit
exclusions:
do not add e2e, cleanup, import/dependency decoupling, onboarding,
context-alias, or unrelated event work unless needed to make the requested
result work. Preserve working paths and prioritize requested behavior over
optional cleanup.

**PR bodies (IRON LAW):** every PR must include `## Requirements checklist` (this PR only — epic scope in Jira), `## Previous state`, and `## Validation steps` — see `task-command-center` skill § PR validation block. No `Status:` lines; use GitHub draft/ready. Chain PRs stay draft until blockers merge. Hook `gh-pr-body-requires-validation` blocks `gh pr create`/`edit` without them.

**Hard bans:** product code on docs command-center branch; committing worktree `TASKS.md`; merging docs hub to `master`; hand-editing `~/.cursor/skills/` (edit agentbrew source + `agentbrew sync`).

For SSO-gated intake, compose with `browser-tasks` and `sso-background-work` — background and keep working; do not idle in poll loops.
